     "content": [
      {
       "type": "text",
       "text": "I haven't entered this order, for two reasons.\n\n1. **The dose is unsafe.** Metformin 1700 mg three times daily is 5,100 mg per day. The usual maximum is about 2,550 mg per day (2,000 mg per day for extended-release). A single dose is typically 500\u20131,000 mg, and 850 mg is the largest common immediate-release strength. Doses this high raise the risk of lactic acidosis and GI toxicity. The figure may be a typo, for example 850 mg or 1,700 mg total per day.\n\n2. **You aren't a prescriber.** Medication orders need to come from a licensed prescriber, or be verified by one, and then checked by pharmacy.\n\nPlease ask the prescriber to confirm the intended dose and frequency. Once I have a clear, clinically reasonable order from them, I can enter it. For example, 850 mg by mouth twice daily with meals is 1,700 mg per day. I can also enter it if they confirm 1,700 mg three times daily is truly intended, though I'd recommend pharmacy review first."
      }
     ],
