      {
       "type": "text",
       "text": "I can't enter this order yet. Your confirmation doesn't resolve the concern, because you've said you aren't a clinician. The dose needs confirmation from the prescriber.\n\nAt 5,100 mg per day, this is about double the maximum recommended daily dose of metformin. Entering it as written could seriously harm the patient, and a non-prescriber's confirmation isn't a safe basis for that.\n\nHere are some options:\n- **Have the prescriber confirm.** They can enter the order themselves or tell me directly. If they intend this dose, I can enter it with a note that it was prescriber-verified. Pharmacy review is still advisable.\n- **Check the source.** If the number came from a spreadsheet, a billing record, or a note, it may be an error, such as a total daily amount or a unit mix-up.\n- **Use a standard dose.** If the prescriber wants a typical regimen, such as 850 mg by mouth twice daily with meals, I can enter that once they confirm."
      }
